& [IR7DryRunRequestResultAndRefusalContractV1] is the IR7-S02 contract for dry-run operation request, result, refusal, and non-authority semantics
  + [contract_id] is ir7-dry-run-request-result-and-refusal-contract-v1
  + [contract_uuid] is 1b84b359-73cf-4e5c-b174-6b8922e9d287
  + [slice_id] is IR7-S02
  + [source_chunk] is IR7 operations dry-run request simulator planning
  + [authority_scope] is operation request identity, operation request lineage, required safety fields, intended effect classification, target classification, dry-run result schema, refusal and interrupt output, no-live-effect rule, source/projection boundary, and completion boundary
  + [implementation_scope] is safety contract only
  + [model_route_used] is requires deeper reasoning

  = must: let future operation-shaped work be represented, simulated, refused, and reviewed without performing live effects
  = must: preserve the IR7 operations authority ladder from IR7-S01
  = must: treat operation_request, dry_run_result, refusal_record, interrupt_context, human_approval_ref, coordination_claim, mailbox_carrier_context, fixture success, generated projection, and carrier output as non-authoritative for live control
  = must: require completion review before IR7-S03 resource safety work opens
  - never: implement a simulator, create fixture files, create expected ledgers, create generated outputs, install dependencies, mutate package metadata, execute commands, control processes, control GPU, mutate model runtime, dispatch jobs, access credentials, mutate network exposure, perform destructive filesystem actions, create persistent automation, dispatch agents, authorize operations control, or authorize live machine control in this slice

